resultant(RingElement,RingElement,RingElement)
**********************************************

  * Function: *note resultant:
    resultant_lpRingElement_cmRingElement_cmRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        resultant(f,g,x)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,
      * g, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in the same
        polynomial ring R as f
      * x, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a variable in R
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Algorithm (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Sylvester
        resultant of f and g with respect to the variable x

Description
===========

The elements f and g should be polynomials in the same ring, and x should be a
variable in that ring.  The result is the determinant of the Sylvester matrix,
sylvesterMatrix(f,g,x).  The resultant of f and its derivative with respect to
x is the discriminant, discriminant(f,x).

